    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "text": "Goucher, Adam P. Gliders in cellular automata on Penrose tilings (2012). Primary paper describing earlier four-state Penrose travelling behaviour under a different update rule.",
      "url": "https://cp4space.hatsya.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/11/2012-penrose-gliders.pdf"
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "text": "Owens, Nick and Stepney, Susan. The Game of Life Rules on Penrose Tilings: still life and oscillators. In A. Adamatzky (ed.), Game of Life Cellular Automata, chapter 18, pp. 331-378. Springer, 2010. Author-maintained catalogue and linked chapter.",
      "url": "https://www-users.york.ac.uk/~ss44/bib/ss/nonstd/penroselife.htm"
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "text": "Stepney, Susan. The Art of Penrose Life. In A. Adamatzky and G. J. Martinez (eds.), Designing Beauty: The Art of Cellular Automata, pp. 103-109. Springer, 2016. DOI: 10.1007/978-3-319-27270-2_15. Figure 6 illustrates the published fireworks oscillator.",
      "url": "https://www-users.york.ac.uk/~ss44/bib/ss/nonstd/AAGoL2016.pdf"
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "text": "Rucker, Rudy and Walker, John. CelLab manual, rule descriptions: Brianâ€™s Brain. Primary software documentation crediting Brian Silvermanâ€™s three-state rule.",
      "url": "https://www.fourmilab.ch/cellab/manual/chap4.html"
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "text": "ConwayLife forum contributors. Hexagonal Generations Rules, topic 1319. Retained dated sources include c0b0p0â€™s 27 February 2014 B2/S1, C=3 rotor and ship (X31, X33), and confocaloidâ€™s 14 October 2024 B246/S246, C=4 gun (X29). Elsewhere this thread is explicitly cited as surveyed background, not evidence of an exact-rule precedent.",
      "url": "https://conwaylife.com/forums/viewtopic.php?f=11&t=1319"
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "text": "ConwayLife forum contributors. Outer-totalistic hexagonal rules with spaceships, topic 3670. Retained records include muzikâ€™s 2019 B245/S35H ship (X27) and John Cerkanâ€™s 15 March 2020 B23/S4H ship (X32). Other uses are marked as surveyed background, not exact-rule predecessors.",
      "url": "https://conwaylife.com/forums/viewtopic.php?f=11&t=3670"
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "text": "Owens, Nick and Stepney, Susan. Investigations of the Game of Life cellular automata rules on Penrose Tilings: lifetime, ash and oscillator statistics. Journal of Cellular Automata 5(3) (2010), 207-225.",
      "url": "https://www-users.york.ac.uk/~ss44/bib/ss/nonstd/jca10.pdf"
    },
    {
      "number": 11,
      "text": "Bays, Carter. A Note on the Game of Life in Hexagonal and Pentagonal Tessellations. Complex Systems 15(3) (2005), 245-252. Earlier hexagonal spaceships, including examples in rules B2/S35 and B245/S3.",
      "url": "https://www.complex-systems.com/abstracts/v15_i03_a04/"
    },
    {
      "number": 12,
      "text": "Smith, David; Myers, Joseph Samuel; Kaplan, Craig S.; and Goodman-Strauss, Chaim. An aperiodic monotile. arXiv:2303.10798, 2023. DOI: 10.48550/arXiv.2303.10798. Primary source for the Hat monotile substrate.",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.10798"
    },
    {
      "number": 13,
      "text": "Gardner, Martin. The fantastic combinations of John Conwayâ€™s new solitaire game â€œlifeâ€. Mathematical Games, Scientific American 223 (October 1970), 120-123. Original account of Conwayâ€™s eight-neighbour, two-state rule; reproduced online.",
      "url": "https://www.ibiblio.org/lifepatterns/october1970.html"
    },
    {
      "number": 14,
      "text": "Golly developers. QuickLife documentation: B/S notation, standard named rules and the B245/S3H hexagonal example. The H suffix denotes a hexagonal neighbourhood, specified separately in this catalogue.",
      "url": "https://golly.sourceforge.io/Help/Algorithms/QuickLife.html"
    },
    {
      "number": 15,
      "text": "ConwayLife forum discussion reached through post 28428. Retained records identify John Cerkanâ€™s 22 January 2016 B2/S35H spaceship RLE (X23), and Dean Hickersonâ€™s 20 January 2016 B2/S34H wall and billiard-table records (X34, X35). The link locates the discussion, not a claim that both authors wrote the linked post. Exact comparisons are retained in research/fixtures/hex-published-provenance.json.",
      "url": "https://conwaylife.com/forums/viewtopic.php?p=28428"
    },
    {
      "number": 16,
      "text": "Naszvadi. B25/S34H puffer, ConwayLife forum post, 1 February 2024. The post also notes earlier knowledge; it is evidence of prior use, not a first-discovery claim.",
      "url": "https://conwaylife.com/forums/viewtopic.php?p=177053#p177053"
    },
    {
      "number": 17,
      "text": "Eppstein, David. Replicators: HighLife. Author-maintained cellular-automaton collection; two-state B36/S23 on the eight-neighbour square grid.",
      "url": "https://ics.uci.edu/~eppstein/ca/replicators/b36s23.html"
    },
    {
      "number": 18,
      "text": "Edmond, James. Interactive Hat and Spectre cellular-automaton project, offlattice.org/monotile. Companion implementation for the published rule tables and travelling behaviours described in the paper [2] and compendium [3].",
      "url": "https://offlattice.org/monotile/"
    },
    {
      "number": 19,
      "text": "Bays, Carter. A Note on the Game of Life in Hexagonal and Pentagonal Tessellations. Complex Systems 15(3) (2005), 245â€“252. Full text of [11]. Figure 3 describes a B2/S35 spaceship; Figure 4 describes a B245/S3 spaceship. The drawings were not independently transcribed: executable seed comparisons for X23 and X24 use Cerkan [15] and Golly [14].",
      "url": "https://wpmedia.wolfram.com/uploads/sites/13/2018/02/15-3-4.pdf"
    },
    {
      "number": 20,
      "text": "drc. Pair of B2/S34H period-48 oscillators. ConwayLife forum, 18 January 2016, post 28430. One independently oscillating six-cell component is reproduced as X28; extracting that component does not make it a new oscillator.",
      "url": "https://conwaylife.com/forums/viewtopic.php?p=28430"
    },
    {
      "number": 21,
      "text": "ConwayLife forum discussion linked in the retained B25/S34H puffer provenance, reached through post 162954. Includes Dmitry Maitakâ€™s report of an earlier occurrence. Used for the publication-history qualification in X30, not as an independently matched seed source.",
      "url": "https://conwaylife.com/forums/viewtopic.php?p=162954"
    },
    {
      "number": 22,
      "text": "ConwayLife forum post 163227 (2023), linked by Dmitry Maitak as an earlier B25/S34H puffer occurrence. Its seed has not been independently compared in this catalogue; see X30. The reported antecedent does not establish first-discovery attribution.",
      "url": "https://conwaylife.com/forums/viewtopic.php?p=163227#p163227"
    },
    {
      "number": 23,
      "text": "ConwayLife forum discussion containing Dean Hickersonâ€™s B2/S34H self-repairing wall and period-2044 billiard-table RLEs, dated 20 January 2016 in the retained provenance. Discussion locator: post 26919. Exact seed comparisons are documented in X34 and X35.",
      "url": "https://conwaylife.com/forums/viewtopic.php?p=26919"
    },
    {
      "number": 24,
      "text": "Silver, Stephen. Life Lexicon, entries â€œblockâ€ and â€œblinkerâ€. Golly 3.2-2 distribution retained by Debian. Pattern descriptions for S01 and S02; the blinker entry credits John H. Conway.",
      "url": "https://sources.debian.org/data/main/g/golly/3.2-2/Help/Lexicon/lex_b.htm"
    },
    {
      "number": 25,
      "text": "Silver, Stephen. Life Lexicon, entries â€œpentadecathlonâ€ and â€œpulsarâ€. Golly 3.2-2 distribution retained by Debian. Pattern descriptions and Conway attribution for S04 and S03 respectively.",
      "url": "https://sources.debian.org/data/main/g/golly/3.2-2/Help/Lexicon/lex_p.htm"
    },
    {
      "number": 26,
      "text": "Silver, Stephen. Life Lexicon, entry â€œgliderâ€. Golly 3.2-2 distribution retained by Debian. Credits Richard K. Guy; source for S05â€™s standard glider and attribution.",
      "url": "https://sources.debian.org/data/main/g/golly/3.2-2/Help/Lexicon/lex_g.htm"
    },
    {
      "number": 27,
      "text": "Silver, Stephen. Life Lexicon, entry â€œLWSSâ€ (lightweight spaceship). Golly 3.2-2 distribution retained by Debian. Credits John H. Conway; source for S06.",
      "url": "https://sources.debian.org/data/main/g/golly/3.2-2/Help/Lexicon/lex_l.htm"
    },
    {
      "number": 28,
      "text": "LifeWiki contributors. â€œOCA:HighLife/Replicatorâ€. Published twelve-cell B36/S23 seed used for S07. Discovery credit to Nathan Thompson (1994) is taken from Eppstein [17].",
      "url": "https://conwaylife.com/wiki/OCA:HighLife/Replicator"
    },
    {
      "number": 29,
      "text": "Silver, Stephen. Life Lexicon, entry â€œdiehardâ€. Golly 3.2-2 distribution retained by Debian. Published seven-cell seed reproduced as S08; this catalogue does not assign an individual discoverer.",
      "url": "https://sources.debian.org/data/main/g/golly/3.2-2/Help/Lexicon/lex_d.htm"
    },
    {
      "number": 30,
      "text": "Silver, Stephen. Life Lexicon, entry â€œR-pentominoâ€. Golly 3.2-2 distribution retained by Debian. Published five-cell configuration reproduced as S09; Gardner [13] provides the contemporary account of Conwayâ€™s investigation.",
      "url": "https://sources.debian.org/data/main/g/golly/3.2-2/Help/Lexicon/lex_r.htm"
    },
    {
      "number": 31,
      "text": "Wainwright, Robert. Lifeline No. 3 (1971), p. 12. Credits the seven-cell Acorn seed to Charles L. Corderman; Wainwright supplied the name. The configuration is reproduced as S10.",
      "url": "https://conwaylife.com/wiki/Lifeline_Volume_3"
    },
    {
      "number": 32,
      "text": "Silver, Stephen. Life Lexicon, entry â€œacornâ€. Golly 3.2-2 distribution retained by Debian. Published seed for S10; the contemporary authorship source is Wainwright [31].",
      "url": "https://sources.debian.org/data/main/g/golly/3.2-2/Help/Lexicon/lex_a.htm"
    },
    {
      "number": 33,
      "text": "Golly developers. Generations algorithm documentation. Defines the refractory-state update and lists named rule templates, including Brianâ€™s Brain and Star Wars. This is framework documentation unless a specific named template is identified at the point of citation.",
      "url": "https://golly.sourceforge.io/Help/Algorithms/Generations.html"
    },
    {
      "number": 34,
      "text": "Griffeath, David, and Moore, Cristopher. Life Without Death is P-complete. Complex Systems 10 (1996), 437â€“447. Published study of the square-grid rule used as template U06; this citation does not identify its first inventor.",
      "url": "https://www.complex-systems.com/abstracts/v10_i06_a03/"
    }
